{"source_key":"sha256-767aea33d36d18c60bf3118db432de90","record_index":245,"record_hash":"sha256:b4600709eebe4be41f253f4eb7f7939a57b5b8184ddbf4972cb426cc410409bb","timestamp":"2026-07-23T14:40:52.275Z","kind":"tool_result","source_event_kind":"codex:response_item:function_call_output","role":null,"text":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"[REDACTED:path]\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"[REDACTED:path]\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"The smallest correct boundary is: carry the stable active-worktree name in `but_graph::init::WorktreeTip`, then let `Editor::create()` consume `workspace.graph.options.worktree_tips`. This gives every editor the feature-gated visible set without changing 27 production construction sites.\\n\\nCurrent flow:\\n\\n- `Context::worktrees_with_state()` is the visibility authority. It is flag-gated, performs adoption/archive reconciliation, and returns stable name, path, symbolic ref if any, and peeled HEAD: `crates/but-ctx/src/worktrees.rs:10-24,46-95`.\\n- `Context::active_worktrees()` filters archived entries: `crates/but-ctx/src/worktrees.rs:97-109`.\\n- `Context::graph_options()` maps only active worktrees into traversal tips: `crates/but-ctx/src/worktrees.rs:26-44`.\\n- `Context::workspace_from_head()` uses those options: `crates/but-ctx/src/lib.rs:780-789`.\\n- `WorktreeTip` currently retains only `ref_name` and commit `id`, losing the stable worktree name needed to reopen its repository: `crates/but-graph/src/init/mod.rs:487-509`.\\n- Graph options are retained on `Graph`, including through retraversal: `crates/but-graph/src/lib.rs:269-274`.\\n- Do not infer visibility from `RefInfo.worktree`: graph annotation enumerates every physical linked worktree independently of archive state: `crates/but-graph/src/init/overlay.rs:347-450`.\\n\\nEditor behavior today:\\n\\n- `GraphEditorOptions` only supports extra mutable refs: `crates/but-rebase/src/graph_rebase/creation.rs:13-33`.\\n- Mutability begins at main HEAD plus `extra_mutable_refs`: `creation.rs:64-87`.\\n- Every graph segment is represented, but non-HEAD/non-extra segments are immutable: `creation.rs:90-167`.\\n- Checkout tracking has only `Checkout::Head`: `crates/but-rebase/src/graph_rebase/mod.rs:245-277`.\\n- Creation records only main HEAD, with the existing TODO calling out owned worktrees: `creation.rs:307-323`.\\n- `Editor::rebase()` co\n[TRUNCATED]\ny retarget that worktree’s checkout marker to the new selector. There is no branch ref that can move automatically.\\n- Never invent or attach a branch implicitly.\\n- If detached manipulation is deferred, fail the mutation before any ref/index/filesystem change with an explicit “detached worktree manipulation is not supported” error.\\n\\nGiven the reported `origin/master` Codex scenario, detached behavior should be an acceptance decision for GB-1753, not a follow-up discovered after branch-backed tests pass.\\n\\n## Minimal test set\\n\\n1. **Branch-backed happy path and attachment invariant**\\n\\n   Rewrite a visible linked branch with unrelated dirt. Assert the branch moves, index/files match the new tree, dirt survives, and the linked `HEAD` file remains exactly `ref: refs/heads/<branch>`.\\n\\n2. **Prepare-all-before-mutation**\\n\\n   Two visible linked worktrees; the second has overlapping dirt. Assert failure leaves every ref, both private HEAD files, both indexes, and both working trees byte-for-byte unchanged.\\n\\n3. **Feature boundary and ref protection**\\n\\n   Without worktree tips, no linked checkout occurs. Separately, deleting an editor reference checked out in any worktree must retain that ref even with the feature flag off.\\n\\n4. **Detached Codex scenario**\\n\\n   Create the worktree from `origin/master` and first assert it is detached. Then either:\\n\\n   - supported: advance detached HEAD to the rewritten/new commit, keep `origin/master` unchanged, and synchronize index/files; or\\n   - deferred: assert a specific pre-mutation error and unchanged